  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Members must stop using damaged tools; a marked tray and repair card keep them separate from tools available for use.\", \"decision\": \"How should a damaged tool be reported?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers place damaged tools in the marked tray and complete repair cards describing what happened during use. The steward receives both the isolated tool and firsthand observations when arranging its inspection.\nMembers isolate damaged tools with brief repair cards, and the steward asks follow-up questions during the next bench round. Unsafe equipment leaves circulation immediately while fuller diagnosis waits for a convenient conversation.\nMembers bring damaged tools to the steward, who asks about the problem and completes repair cards before isolating them. A short conversation captures details that may be difficult to describe on an unattended form."
    }
  ],
